{"id": "EUVD-2026-107695", "enisaUuid": "73705af5-0eb7-35ac-8f49-043a01a55615", "description": "Roundcube Webmail before 1.6.20 and 1.7.x before 1.7.5 is affected by a path traversal vulnerability in the squirrelmail_usercopy plugin. With the file based backend, the source path was built from the login name without rejecting path separators, so a login name containing a slash could cause files outside the configured squirrelmail_data_dir to be read and imported. Upstream fixed this in the commit \u201cFix unsafe use of a login name in SquirrelMail import file path\u201d, which rejects login names containing a slash.", "datePublished": "2026-10-22T01:08:34", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T01:08:34", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N", "references": ["https://bugs.debian.org/1151279", "https://github.com/roundcube/roundcubemail/commit/dbdfcac498164bcacb7ce273b6341678dd70c166", "https://roundcube.net/news/2026/10/19/security-updates-1.6.20-and-1.7.5", "https://github.com/roundcube/roundcubemail/releases/tag/1.7.5", "https://github.com/roundcube/roundcubemail/releases/tag/1.6.20", "https://github.com/roundcube/roundcubemail/commit/15fd175d154311ca7f59cf696c6cc39471611aa6"], "aliases": ["GHSA-748m-7gjm-2xw3", "CVE-2026-114714"], "assigner": "mitre", "epss": 0.37, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2c289d40-f41e-3a83-8221-3e2816cf4516", "product": {"name": "Webmail", "vendor": {"name": "bulwarkmail"}}, "product_version": "1.7.0 <1.7.5"}, {"id": "e271d543-02d1-36f1-b46d-116ed1fd617b", "product": {"name": "Webmail", "vendor": {"name": "bulwarkmail"}}, "product_version": "1.6.0 <1.6.20"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a9d714fe-fecd-3ebc-bb26-b893113e7218", "vendor": {"name": "Roundcube"}}], "isExploited": false}